   "v": "sasha",
   "t": "Я не хотела, правда.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'I didn't mean to, honestly.' A compact expression built around 'I' and 'honestly'.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "sasha",
   "t": "Я сейчас все вытру.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'I will wipe it all up now.' The key word here means 'I', which Sasha combines with 'now'.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "anya",
   "t": "Не надо плакать.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'Don't cry.' Here 'it is necessary' sets up the idea, while 'to cry' comes at the end for emphasis.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "anya",
   "t": "Все хорошо.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'Everything is fine.' You'll hear 'good' all the time in the show, here connected with 'good'.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "sasha",
   "t": "Вы меня уволите?",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'Will you fire me?' Notice the word order: 'you' comes first, and 'will fire' finishes the sentence.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "sasha",
   "t": "Вы расскажете все руководству.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'You will tell management everything.' Sasha starts with 'you' and pairs it with 'will tell' to make the point clear. And Max jumps in.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "anya",
   "t": "Никуда я не пойду.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'I am not going anywhere.' Max puts 'nowhere' up front so the listener immediately catches the tone, followed by 'I'.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "anya",
   "t": "Ничего я не скажу.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'I won't say anything.' In Russian, 'nothing' leads into 'I'll tell' in a very natural everyday phrasing.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "sasha",
   "t": "Извините меня.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'Excuse me.' In Russian, 'sorry' leads into 'me' in a very natural everyday phrasing.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "sasha",
   "t": "Я правда не хотела.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'I really didn't mean to.' The key word here means 'I', which Sasha combines with 'honestly'.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "anya",
   "t": "Успокойся.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
